%% Eraser lifecycle state diagram
stateDiagram-v2
  [*] --> Idle

  state "Idle / no eraser session" as Idle
  note right of Idle
    No eraser corridor, candidate cache, overlay preview,
    or eraser-owned commit intent exists. Generic pointer
    session owns down admission and one active routing token.
  end note

  Idle --> DownAdmission: generic pointer session admits finite normalized down
  Idle --> Disposed: runtime.dispose()
  Idle --> Idle: stale move/up/cancel or invalid down / no eraser session

  state "Down admitted by pointer session" as DownAdmission
  note right of DownAdmission
    Admission requires the active token, session id, controllerEpoch,
    draw mode, eraser tool, finite point, and finite thickness.
    Pointer id is only the routing token.
  end note

  DownAdmission --> Previewing: bind eraser session; freeze first corridor point; publish visual preview
  DownAdmission --> Idle: wrong mode/tool or non-finite facts / reject without preview
  DownAdmission --> Disposed: disposed runtime / StateError

  state "Active eraser preview" as Previewing {
    [*] --> CorridorPreview

    state "Overlay corridor preview" as CorridorPreview
    note right of CorridorPreview
      Corridor points are immutable snapshots of one retained world-space
      approximation only. Each admitted move appends before any resample,
      freezes one retained snapshot, and updates overlay repaint only.
      Down and moves perform no scene read, envelope, spatial query, candidate resolution,
      exact hit, or deletion projection.
    end note

    CorridorPreview --> CorridorPreview: same-token same-controllerEpoch finite move / admit one point; resample 8001 to 4000 if needed; publish visual snapshot
    CorridorPreview --> CorridorPreview: stale token, controllerEpoch mismatch, or non-finite move / ignore
    CorridorPreview --> TerminalGate: same-token up
    CorridorPreview --> CleanupOnly: same-token cancel
    CorridorPreview --> CleanupOnly: mode change
    CorridorPreview --> CleanupOnly: interactive=false
    CorridorPreview --> CleanupOnly: loadDocument prepared cleanup before install
    CorridorPreview --> CorridorPreview: loadDocumentFromJson failure / preserve if pointer session preserves
    CorridorPreview --> CleanupOnly: runtime.dispose()

    state "Terminal up gate" as TerminalGate
    note right of TerminalGate
      Terminal commit is allowed only for same token, same controllerEpoch,
      finite terminal point, and candidate/geometry facts derived
      from the final corridor. Terminal budget is 4096 candidates /
      32768 exact checks.
    end note

    TerminalGate --> CleanupOnly: stale token, controllerEpoch mismatch, non-finite, or invalid terminal
    TerminalGate --> FinalCandidates: valid terminal / admit endpoint; resample if needed; one immutable snapshot and one terminal read

    state "Final candidate and geometry check" as FinalCandidates
    FinalCandidates --> EraseDecision: compute erased ids from valid deletable content candidates
    FinalCandidates --> CleanupOnly: budget exceeded / cleanup no-op, no partial erase

    state EraseDecision <<choice>>
    EraseDecision --> CleanupOnly: erased ids empty
    EraseDecision --> PreparedResolver: erased ids non-empty

    state "Prepared deletion resolver" as PreparedResolver
    note right of PreparedResolver
      RuntimeRoot prepares the sparse document, Store revision/id binding,
      selection backing, revision, delivery, and erase action inputs before
      calling the required guarded resolver with canonical Store entries.
      Preparation failure has no callback and enters cleanup.
    end note

    PreparedResolver --> AcceptedInstall: resolver accepts
    PreparedResolver --> CleanupOnly: resolver cancels or throws / discard

    state "Single-use accepted install" as AcceptedInstall
    note right of AcceptedInstall
      The private prepared value consumes once: Store installs its bound
      sparse document and ledgers, then Selection installs its owned backing.
      No normal failure, callback, publication, retry, or rollback lies
      between those two owner installs.
    end note

    AcceptedInstall --> CleanupBeforeSignals: accepted Store then Selection

    state "Cleanup before public state" as CleanupBeforeSignals
    note right of CleanupBeforeSignals
      Eraser action and state/repaint notifications are
      published only after successful commit and coordinator-owned
      session cleanup.
    end note

    CleanupBeforeSignals --> CleanupCoordinator: post-success cleanup request

    state "Publish erase action and runtime state" as PublishCommitSignals
    PublishCommitSignals --> [*]: publish main repaint, overlay cleanup, CanvasRuntimeState, erase action

    state "Cleanup only" as CleanupOnly
    note left of CleanupOnly
      Cancel, mode change, prepared load cleanup, interactive=false,
      dispose, stale or invalid terminal, empty erased ids,
      eraser budget exceeded with no partial erase,
      resolver cancel/error and preparation failure create typed cleanup requests for
      preview/session only.
      Empty/no-op cleanup publishes no erase action or document
      state. Active preview cleanup publishes CanvasRuntimeState
      with updated preview revision.
    end note

    CleanupOnly --> CleanupCoordinator: typed cleanup request

    state "PointerToolCleanupCoordinator" as CleanupCoordinator
    note left of CleanupCoordinator
      Coordinator-owned eraser cleanup clears corridor,
      candidates, token binding, and session facts and returns
      an effect-only PointerCleanupOutcome. It does not run exact
      eraser checks, open edits, emit erase actions, or publish
      document state directly.
    end note

    CleanupCoordinator --> CleanupOverlay: outcome repaint target is overlay

    state "Overlay cleanup repaint" as CleanupOverlay
    CleanupOverlay --> [*]: request overlay repaint only from coordinator-owned outcome
    CleanupOverlay --> PublishCommitSignals: accepted install effects after cleanup
  }

  Previewing --> Idle: eraser session closed
  Previewing --> Disposed: dispose cleanup complete

  state "Disposed runtime" as Disposed
  Disposed --> Disposed: pointer input or mutating operation / StateError

  note left of Previewing
    Forbidden paths:
    no selected-move resolver;
    no main-scene preview during eraser preview;
    no direct DocumentStoreKernel mutation;
    no full committed mutation during preview;
    no partial erase on budget exceeded;
  end note
